The library helper below is called once:
function label(x = 605) { return x; }
console.log(label());
In this run, what is printed when no argument is passed?

One engineer hands another the following code:
const n = 606;
console.log(n == '606');
Explain what this code prints and why that value follows from the language rules.

Study the program and name its final output:
